letitedit: mlt_chain_attach_normalizers releases the reference mlt_factory_link gave each normalizer link once the
chain holds its own (mlt_chain_attach), so a clip's links are freed with the clip instead of living for the rest of
the process (about 377 Windows handles and the links' scalers and resamplers per clip). From
engine-patches/mlt-chain-normalizer-ref; applies on MLT 63218a28d21f1e64b5b9e6671b4ff9146023282c (the framework,
libmlt-7.dll).

diff --git a/src/framework/mlt_chain.c b/src/framework/mlt_chain.c
index fafb93db..aa3137a3 100644
--- a/src/framework/mlt_chain.c
+++ b/src/framework/mlt_chain.c
@@ -476,6 +476,9 @@ extern void mlt_chain_attach_normalizers(mlt_chain self)
                 mlt_properties_set_int(MLT_LINK_PROPERTIES(link), "_loader", 1);
                 mlt_chain_attach(self, link);
                 mlt_chain_move_link(self, mlt_chain_link_count(self) - 1, norm_count);
+                // The chain holds its own reference now (mlt_chain_attach): release the factory's, as every other
+                // caller of mlt_chain_attach does, or the link outlives the chain.
+                mlt_link_close(link);
                 norm_count++;
                 break;
             }
